<p class="mt-indent-1 lt-chem-408745">a) The formal charge on any one&nbsp;\(\mathrm{C}\) atom is 0. How many sigma and pi bonds must each carbon be forming?</p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong>Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p class="lt-chem-408745">There has to be a double bond associated with each carbon for it to be forming 4 bonds and have 0 formal charge, so each carbon is forming 3 sigma bonds and 1 pi bond</p>
    </dd>
</dl>

<p class="mt-indent-1 lt-chem-408745">b) Is VSEPR satisfied? Is it almost satisfied?</p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong>Answer</strong></dt>
