<dl>
    <dt><strong>Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p class="lt-chem-408745">Methanol has the least vapor pressure because its \(\mathrm{OH}\) group allows it to hydrogen bond to other methanol molecules. Next is hexane because, though it does not have hydrogen bonding capabilities, it is more linear than isooctane so can experience greater London dispersion forces. Isooctane has the highest vapor pressure because it has no hydrogen bonding capability and is less stackable than hexane so it has less London dispersion forces present.</p>
    </dd>
